cff-version: 1.2.0
title: toothpaste-kit
message: If you use this project or its orchestration protocol in your work, please cite it.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A skill library and agent relay protocol for working with large language model
  agents, judged on control fidelity: legible state, cheap correction, a reliable
  halt. Includes a vendor-independent capability taxonomy, a message schema for
  relaying work between agents and humans across surfaces, and a routing rule that
  gates dispatch on content sensitivity.
authors:
  - family-names: Naveja
    given-names: Aidan
repository-code: https://github.com/AN0099/toothpaste-kit
url: https://github.com/AN0099/toothpaste-kit
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - agent-orchestration
  - human-in-the-loop
  - provenance
  - research-software
  - accessibility

version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-19'

# These two were commented out until a release existed, because a file claiming
# a released version that does not exist is worse than one claiming nothing.
# They are filled in as step 3 of docs/releasing.md. THIS COMMIT MUST BE THE
# COMMIT THAT GETS TAGGED v0.1.0. If it is committed and not tagged, this file
# is the lie it was written to avoid.
#
# The identifiers block comes after the release exists, because Zenodo mints the
# DOI from the GitHub release rather than the other way round. Filled in
# 2026-09-19 once the release was published.
#
# The concept DOI is listed first and is the one to cite: it covers every
# version and always resolves to the newest. The version DOI is kept beside it
# so a reader citing this exact release has the identifier for it.

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22850481
    description: Concept DOI, all versions, resolves to the newest
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22850482
    description: Version DOI for v0.1.0
